      "parent_ids": [
        "02238edf92978091d114041a35c9db16604296d9"
      ],
      "title": "extcap: Fix of handling default values",
      "message": "extcap: Fix of handling default values\n\nPatch fixes the issue when default mandatory parameter has default\nvalue. It was not possible to start a capture.\n\nChanges:\nTo clarify reason of calling extcap_has_configuration() I created\nextcap_has_configuration() and extcap_requires_configuration().\nextcap_has_configuration() returns TRUE when extcap has any settings and\nmakes sense to show extcap settings dialog.\nextcap_requires_configuration() returns TRUE when extcap configuration\nis not complete and it is required to finish it.\n\nextcap_requires_configuration() was modified to handle mandatory parameter with default value correctly.\n\nextcap_options_dialog correctly stores settings in memory even 'Save\nsettings ...' checkbox is unchecked.\n\nFixed issues in storing bool/boolflag values.\n\nFixes: 18487\n",
      "author_name": "Jirka Novak",
      "author_email": "j.novak@netsystem.cz",
      "authored_date": "2023-01-29T16:12:28.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Gerald Combs",
      "committer_email": "gerald@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2023-02-06T18:28:58.000+00:00",
